# ==============================================================================
# IT 140 AUTOMATION PSEUDOSCRIPT TEMPLATE
# ==============================================================================
#
# Repository path:
#  scripts/.dev/pseudoscripts/template_it140.pseudo
#
# Purpose:
#  Define the common structure and writing style for the platform-agnostic
#  IT 140 automation pseudoscripts.
#
# Covered artifacts:
#  prepare_it140.pseudo
#  install_it140.pseudo
#  configure_it140.pseudo
#  update_it140.pseudo
#  verify_it140.pseudo
#
# Artifact version: 0.10.0-beta.1
# Version date-time group: 2026-08-09-23-59
# Development status: Beta Testing
#
# Version basis:
#  Version 0.1.0 represents the initial template baseline. Version 0.2.0 adds
#  the artifact version, version date, and development-status standard.
#  Version 0.3.0 adds the common CVD course-continuity conclusion.
#  Version 0.4.0 adds repository-workspace ownership and desktop-integration rules.
#
# Repository baseline:
#  GC-STEM/it140 commit dbde859f90b1b957b05aa03e25b867563c113bb2
#
# Authority:
#  The current SRS, SDD, controlled manifest, manifest schema, and tested
#  platform implementations remain authoritative. A pseudoscript records
#  platform-agnostic logic; it does not replace those controlled artifacts.
#
# ==============================================================================


# ==============================================================================
# 1. PSEUDOSCRIPT CLASSES
# ==============================================================================
#
# BOOTSTRAP COMMAND SET
# ---------------------
#
# prepare_it140.pseudo represents commands that a user manually copies and
# pastes before the controlled manifest and lifecycle scripts are available.
#
# Bootstrap:
#  - does not use the lifecycle-script main procedure;
#  - does not require the manifest or schema;
#  - does not acquire a lifecycle mutation lock;
#  - does not install or update the course IDE;
#  - creates a lifecycle transcript;
#  - retrieves a clean snapshot of the course repository;
#  - overlays repository files into the course root without deleting
#    unrelated existing course content;
#  - removes repository metadata from the downloaded snapshot and course root;
#  - makes the matching student lifecycle scripts executable;
#  - adds the matching script directory to the shell PATH persistently and
#    to the current shell session.
#
# MANAGED LIFECYCLE SCRIPTS
# -------------------------
#
# install_it140.pseudo, configure_it140.pseudo, update_it140.pseudo, and verify_it140.pseudo
# use the managed lifecycle-script pattern below.
#
# install:
#  state_scope       = system
#  may_change_state  = TRUE
#  lock_required     = TRUE
#  privilege_model   = standard user with approved operation-level elevation
#  normal_next_step  = configure
#
# Repository-workspace rule:
#  - configure may create the ~/Repos parent and explicitly course-owned desktop integration;
#  - configure never recursively mutates workspace children;
#  - verify observes workspace integration read-only;
#  - prepare, install, and update do not own repository-workspace repair.
#
# configure:
#  state_scope       = current_user
#  may_change_state  = TRUE
#  lock_required     = TRUE
#  privilege_model   = standard user; reject elevated execution
#  normal_next_step  = verify
#
# update:
#  state_scope       = system_and_course_managed_user_state
#  may_change_state  = TRUE
#  lock_required     = TRUE
#  privilege_model   = standard user with approved operation-level elevation
#  normal_next_step  = configure for first use; otherwise verify
#
# verify:
#  state_scope       = read_only_observation
#  may_change_state  = FALSE
#  lock_required     = FALSE
#  privilege_model   = standard user; never elevate
#  normal_next_step  = no action or the reported remediation
#
# ==============================================================================


# ==============================================================================
# 2. ARTIFACT VERSION STANDARD
# ==============================================================================
#
# Apply Semantic Versioning (SemVer) 2.0.0 to every distributed or testable
# artifact.
#
# Required artifact metadata:
#  artifact_version   = MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
#  version_date       = YYYY-MM-DD
#  development_status = approved development-status label
#
# Version date:
#  - records when that exact artifact version was created;
#  - changes whenever the artifact version changes;
#  - remains separate from the artifact version;
#  - does not affect version precedence.
#
# Development status:
#  - records the artifact's current lifecycle stage separately from SemVer;
#  - uses an approved repository status such as Construction, Alpha Testing,
#    Beta Testing, Release Review, or Ready for Production;
#  - does not determine whether MINOR or PATCH changes;
#  - requires a new PATCH version if an embedded status value is changed in an
#    artifact that has already been distributed or identified for testing.
#
# Artifact contract:
#  Treat filenames, commands, options, supported platforms, lifecycle workflow,
#  exit codes, managed files and directories, required prompts, stable log fields,
#  and documented behavior as the public interface for versioning decisions.
#
# Initial development:
#  - Use major version 0 while the artifact contract is unstable.
#  - Begin a new artifact at 0.1.0.
#  - Increment MINOR and reset PATCH to 0 when adding functionality or making a
#    meaningful backward-compatible change to behavior or the artifact contract.
#  - Increment PATCH when correcting or clarifying the existing functional
#    baseline without adding functionality or changing the artifact contract.
#  - A breaking change may increment MINOR while the artifact remains below 1.0.0;
#    document the changed contract clearly because 0.y.z is not stable.
#
# Stable releases:
#  - Version 1.0.0 establishes the stable artifact contract.
#  - Increment PATCH for backward-compatible corrections.
#  - Increment MINOR and reset PATCH to 0 for backward-compatible functionality
#    or deprecations.
#  - Increment MAJOR and reset MINOR and PATCH to 0 for incompatible changes.
#
# Small changes:
#  - Do not change the version for comments, spelling, punctuation, or formatting
#    edits made only in an unreleased working copy.
#  - Increment PATCH when redistributing an identified artifact after correcting
#    code, comments, user-facing text, or embedded metadata.
#  - Cosmetic corrections may be bundled into the next planned release instead
#    of creating a standalone release.
#
# Release immutability:
#  - Never modify the contents of an already distributed version in place.
#  - Any changed artifact redistributed for testing or use requires a new version.
#  - Git commits record development activity; they do not automatically require
#    version changes unless they create a new distributed or testable artifact.
#
# Version format:
#  - Use only MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH for routine artifact versions.
#  - Do not encode a calendar date in the artifact version.
#  - Do not use prerelease or build identifiers unless the repository later
#    adopts and documents a specific need for them.
#
# ==============================================================================


# ==============================================================================
# 3. STYLE STANDARD
# ==============================================================================
#
# Use uppercase control words:
#
#  BEGIN
#  END
#  PROCEDURE
#  RETURN
#  IF
#  ELSE IF
#  ELSE
#  ENDIF
#  FOR EACH
#  ENDFOR
#  TRY
#  CATCH
#  FINALLY
#  ENDTRY
#
# Use descriptive lower_snake_case identifiers.
#
# Use dotted identifiers for stages and checks:
#
#  run.initialize
#  platform.validate
#  manifest.validate
#  setup.system_software
#  configure.provider_identity
#  update.course_assets
#  verify.user_path
#  run.summary
#  run.course_continuity.local
#  run.course_continuity.cvd
#
# Layout:
#  - Indent nested blocks by four spaces.
#  - Put one logical operation or decision on each line.
#  - Use LF line endings and no tabs.
#  - Keep lines at 100 characters or fewer when practical.
#  - Move repeated or complex logic into a named procedure.
#
# Platform independence:
#  - Express intent through logical operations and platform adapters.
#  - Do not embed package-manager, shell, desktop, or provider commands.
#  - Obtain required products, packages, settings, assets, and policy values
#    from the validated manifest whenever the manifest is available.
#  - Bootstrap-only values come from controlled implementation constants
#    because bootstrap runs before the manifest is installed locally.
#
# Communication:
#  - Use INFO, SUCCESS, NOTICE, WARNING, and ERROR labels.
#  - Do not rely on color.
#  - Use clear adult-learner language.
#  - State the current stage, result, and next required user action.
#  - Do not expose secrets or unnecessary personal information.
#
# ==============================================================================


# ==============================================================================
# 4. COMMON LIFECYCLE-SCRIPT INITIALIZATION
# ==============================================================================

PROCEDURE initialize_managed_lifecycle_run(action_id, arguments)

    enable_strict_error_handling()
    set_private_default_file_permissions()

    options = parse_action_options_before_logging(arguments)

    IF options.help_requested = TRUE
        display_help_without_creating_log()
        RETURN exit_code_0
    ENDIF

    IF options.version_requested = TRUE
        display_version_without_creating_log(
            script_version = implementation_script_version(),
            version_date = implementation_version_date(),
            development_status = implementation_development_status()
        )
        RETURN exit_code_0
    ENDIF

    run_context = resolve_home_derived_paths(
        course_root = "${HOME}/it140",
        script_root = "${HOME}/it140/scripts",
        manifest_path = "${HOME}/it140/scripts/.manifest/it140_manifest.json",
        schema_path = "${HOME}/it140/scripts/.manifest/it140_manifest.schema.json",
        log_directory = "${HOME}/it140/logs",
        platform_id = implementation_platform_id(),
        deployment_profile_id = options.deployment_profile
    )

    create_private_log_directory(run_context.log_directory)
    start_timestamped_transcript(
        filename_pattern = "<action>_<platform>_<YYYYMMDD>_<HHMMSS>.log"
    )

    install_action_error_handlers()
    install_action_interruption_handlers()
    install_action_cleanup_handler_when_required()

    display_opening_information(
        action_id,
        script_version = implementation_script_version(),
        version_date = implementation_version_date(),
        development_status = implementation_development_status(),
        current_user = sanitized_current_user_id(),
        purpose = action_purpose(),
        log_path = run_context.log_path
    )

    RETURN run_context

ENDPROCEDURE


# ==============================================================================
# 5. COMMON MANIFEST VALIDATION
# ==============================================================================

PROCEDURE validate_controlled_manifest_pair(
    manifest_path,
    schema_path,
    platform_id,
    deployment_profile_id,
    required_top_level_keys
)

    REQUIRE manifest_path and schema_path are readable
    PARSE both files as UTF-8 JSON while rejecting duplicate keys
    REQUIRE manifest schema_version is supported
    REQUIRE schema declares approved JSON Schema draft
    REQUIRE required_top_level_keys are present
    REQUIRE operating-system release upgrades are prohibited when applicable
    REQUIRE platform exists and is enabled
    REQUIRE deployment profile exists, is enabled, and references platform_id
    REQUIRE platform facts required by the implementation match the profile

    IF an approved schema-validation library is available
        VALIDATE the manifest against the schema
    ENDIF

    RETURN manifest.automation_release

ENDPROCEDURE


# ==============================================================================
# 6. COMMON MUTATION SAFETY
# ==============================================================================

PROCEDURE acquire_shared_mutation_lock(action_id, platform_id)

    IF the platform provides a nonblocking file-lock capability
        ACQUIRE the shared IT 140 platform mutation lock
        IF the lock is already held
            DISPLAY ERROR that another conflicting IT 140 operation is running
            RETURN failure
        ENDIF
    ENDIF

    RETURN success

ENDPROCEDURE


PROCEDURE preserve_unrelated_user_content(target, managed_changes)

    READ the existing target when valid
    MERGE only managed keys or managed blocks
    WRITE to a temporary file in the same directory
    VALIDATE the temporary file
    ATOMICALLY replace the target
    REMOVE temporary data

    IF the existing target is invalid
        PRESERVE the original target unchanged
        WRITE only a content-free diagnostic to the private log directory
        RETURN failure
    ENDIF

    RETURN success

ENDPROCEDURE


PROCEDURE display_course_continuity_guidance(execution_context)

    IF execution_context identifies the CVD deployment profile
        DISPLAY: Course continuity: This issue affects the Codio Virtual Desktop (CVD). Follow the remediation above. If the issue continues, contact course support and include the log file.
    ELSE
        DISPLAY: Course continuity: You can continue your IT 140 coursework in the Codio Virtual Desktop (CVD) while this local course IDE issue is resolved.
    ENDIF

ENDPROCEDURE


PROCEDURE finish_mutating_action(result, run_context, changed, warnings, failures)

    DETERMINE exit code:
        0 = completed successfully
        1 = required operation failed before managed state changed
        2 = invalid invocation or unsupported execution context
        3 = required privilege unavailable
        4 = required network or source retrieval failed
        5 = manifest, schema, or controlled-configuration failure
        6 = user canceled before managed state changed
        7 = partial result or failure after managed state changed

    DISPLAY summary with:
        result
        script version
        version date
        development status
        manifest release when available
        warnings
        failures
        restart guidance when applicable
        elapsed time
        next step
        log path
        exit code

    DISPLAY NOTICE with the log path

    IF resolved exit code is nonzero OR result is noncompliant
        CALL display_course_continuity_guidance(run_context)
    ENDIF

    DISPLAY NOTICE to close the current terminal after reviewing the summary
    DISPLAY NOTICE to open a new terminal before another script or command

    RETURN resolved exit code

ENDPROCEDURE


# ==============================================================================
# 7. VERIFY RESULT STANDARD
# ==============================================================================

PROCEDURE record_verification_result(status, check_id, message, remediation = NONE)

    REQUIRE status is one of:
        pass
        warning
        fail
        not_applicable

    DISPLAY "[STATUS] [check_id] message"
    INCREMENT the matching status count

    IF status = fail AND remediation is not empty
        ADD remediation once to the recommended-action collection
    ENDIF

ENDPROCEDURE


# ==============================================================================
# 8. CURRENT CVD ALIGNMENT CHECKLIST
# ==============================================================================
#
# A platform implementation aligned with the tested Codio Virtual Desktop (CVD)
# baseline must preserve these lifecycle boundaries:
#
#  - bootstrap retrieves the repository but performs no IDE maintenance;
#  - install_it140.sh is admin/SME-facing and remains outside student updates;
#  - update synchronizes only the student config, update, and verify scripts;
#  - configure owns provider identity and current-user personalization;
#  - verify is read-only except for its transcript and an explicitly approved
#    sanitized support bundle;
#  - update never performs an operating-system release upgrade;
#  - optional Num Lock convenience failures never block course readiness;
#  - every managed lifecycle script ends with log and fresh-terminal notices.
#
# ==============================================================================
